## h i g h l i g h t s
Metal and metal compound heterojunction embeded in N-doped nanofiber is developed.   
Modification of heterojunction improves the ORR performance.   
· ${\mathsf{C o}}/{\mathsf{C o S}}_{2}@N.$ -CNF modified MFC demonstrates high power density and stability.   
Wastewater treatment efficiency of the MFC decorated with ${\mathsf{C o}}/{\mathsf{C o S}}_{2}@N-$ CNF is superior.
g r a p h i c a l a b s t r a c t
Zeolitic imidazolate framework derived metal and metal compound heterojunction embeded in N-doped carbon nanofiber is developed via employing electrospinning, in-situ growth and subsequent annealing strategies. Benefit from the coupled heterogeneous interface, functional N configuration, and improved electron/mass transport, the assembled microbial fuel cells present superior electrochemical performance.
